- op: discuss  # bd26
  at: '2026-08-26T16:26:02Z'  # bd26
  by: agent  # bd26
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bd26
  clock: 3  # bd26
  nonce: bd26  # bd26
  message: "STEP 1 (PRICING) IS DONE. Measurement 0008; instrument\nscripts/measure-cross-function-reach.py; raw in\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p5_famig_08262026/json/.\n\nTHE CEILING: 18.3% of cross-function findings (778 of 4,245) meet the NECESSARY\nconditions for a single-hop composed walk -- source function calls the sink's\nfunction directly, and the sink's function carries reaching-def coverage.\nPer-repository median 22.3%, range 0%-100%. Sufficiency additionally needs the\ntainted value to be an ARGUMENT at the call, which is param_to_calls and does not\nexist, so this is a ceiling and the achievable figure is strictly below it.\n\nPER-REPO, because the pooled figure is a beads statistic wearing a cohort's name\n(beads alone is 62.4% of pooled findings -- INV-duvup):\n\n  repo             xf find   1hop+ddg   ceiling\n  ArkLib                 8          8    100.0%\n  beads               2650        565     21.3%\n  cert-manager          30         11     36.7%\n  cilium               953         76      8.0%\n  gocryptfs            400         93     23.2%\n  jaeger                58         20     34.5%\n  kamaraflow             0          -   EXCLUDED  (0 xf findings; all 6 blocked\n                                                   walks stop at\n                                                   source_not_tracked, so its\n                                                   zero measures a DIFFERENT\n                                                   blocker)\n  mobx                   2          0      0.0%\n  plausible              7          5     71.4%\n  session-desktop        7          0      0.0%\n  spacedrive           130          0      0.0%\n  POOLED              4245        778     18.3%\n\n*** THE RESULT THAT DECIDES THIS ITEM, AND IT IS NOT THE CEILING. *** The payoff\nsplits by DIRECTION, and the two halves want different decisions:\n\n  REFUTATION: BOUNDED AT ZERO, AND COMPOSITION DOES NOT MOVE IT. Removal\n  authority can act only on `unconfirmed` -- the walk ran and established no\n  dependence. Over the same 11 repositories, of the 28 walks that RAN:\n  14 confirmed / 14 escaped / ZERO unconfirmed. Composition manufactures running\n  walks; on the observed split those become confirmations and escapes, not the\n  class removal needs. So §4a is NOT the gate on WI-kabif's removal arm that\n  0007's framing implied, and this item should not be sold as unblocking it.\n\n  CONFIRMATION: REAL, AND IT INFLATES THE OUTPUT -- a cost nobody had priced.\n  `analysis_method` is IN the collapse key and adjudicated flows bypass\n  collapse_unadjudicated_flows entirely (taint.py:641). So a newly-confirmed flow\n  becomes ITS OWN ROW while the ddg_mixed group it left behind survives one\n  member lighter. A situation of 40 members with 10 confirmations becomes ELEVEN\n  rows, not one improved one. At the ceiling that is up to 778 new `precise` rows\n  on a cohort that emits 298 rows in total.\n\nDEPTH IS NOT HEADROOM. Only 21.9% of cross-function findings are one hop. The\n56.4% \"whole chain covered\" figure should NOT be pursued: jaeger's 5-hop route\nruns from a _test.go helper through internal/tenancy into examples/hotrod, which\nis not plausibly a real call chain, and each extra hop multiplies exposure to\ncall-graph false edges. Composing along long routes would carry taint down\nfabricated paths.\n\nLANGUAGE: go is 94.2% of findings (ceiling 18.2%), so this cohort is\nsubstantially a Go measurement. python 46.3% and javascript 45.8% are more than\ndouble it on volumes too small to carry weight. rust (130 findings) and\ntypescript (9) return a STRUCTURAL ZERO -- rust has none at one hop and none with\na fully-covered route despite 82 with a covered sink.\n\nTHREE INDEPENDENT RECONCILIATIONS AGAINST 0007, which is why I believe the\ninstrument rather than merely its output: (1) cross-function evidence rows total\n106 against 0007's independently-reported 106; (2) the verdict census reproduces\n0007's result table ROW FOR ROW (14/0/14/139/131, 298 rows); (3) per repository\nthe blockers reconcile to 0007's not_attempted column (beads 58+16=74,\njaeger 9+2=11, ...).\n\nPRE-REGISTRATION SCORED, and it scored badly. Predicted 25-50% (central 35%) of\ncross-function rows becoming running walks. The single-hop ceiling is 18.3%\n(BELOW the band); the all-hops ceiling is 56.4% (above it). THE PRE-REGISTRATION\nWAS UNDERSPECIFIED -- it never named a composition DEPTH, so it does not\nadjudicate between them. Its own invalidation section says \"the 1-hop figure is\nthe one to trust\", and under that reading the prediction was too optimistic. The\ntripwire (suspect a much LARGER number) did NOT fire; the number is smaller, in\nthe direction of less payoff, and three reconciliations corroborate the\npopulation.\n\nWHAT STEPS 2-3 SHOULD NOW BE. NOT \"build param_to_calls to unblock removal\" --\nthat is refuted above. If §4a is built at all it is a LABELLING change, and it\nmust be priced against the row-inflation cost before, not after. The single\nnumber most worth re-checking first is the 0-of-28 unconfirmed rate: it is\nconsistent across every repository and across 0007's independent run, but 28\nwalks is a small base, and \"unconfirmed is 0 among walks that run today\" is not\nthe same claim as \"unconfirmed would be ~0 among walks composition makes run\".\nThat inference is the load-bearing one and it is NOT measured."  # bd26
