  message: "THE SEPARABLE DOCS DEFECT THIS ITEM NAMES IS ALREADY CLOSED -- verified, not assumed. The description ends with: 'DOCS DEFECT FOUND WHILE FILING ... ADR-0017's top-of-file Status line still reads \"§4 function summaries and §7a field-sensitivity are SPECIFIED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED\" ... Fix the Status line to split §4a from §4b when this item lands.'\n\nRead at dev 57af2cc060 today, docs/adr/0017-taint-zone-dataflow.md line 5: the Status line was re-measured 2026-08-26 on dev daafb0abb1 and now splits them exactly as asked -- '§4b declared summaries LIVE (declared terminating entries reach _use_site_terminates ...)' against '§4a inferred summaries IMPLEMENTED BUT UNWIRED (infer_summary, zero production callers -- and the shipped dataclass lacks the param_to_calls / param_to_param this subsection specifies, WI-famig)'. It also does the thing this item asked for and more: it names the distinction in terms ('\"Not implemented\" tells a reader to WRITE it; \"implemented but unwired\" tells them to WIRE it -- those are different jobs'), and it declines to pin a §4b count because the catalogue size moved 33 -> 108 -> 113 in two days.\n\nSo that line of work carries INV-lataj's fix, filed and landed independently of this item on the same day this item was filed. NOTHING IS OWED HERE. Removing it from the item's tail so the next reader does not spend the trip.\n\nThe item's remaining scope is unchanged and is NOT an implementation: step 1 (pricing) shipped as measurement 0008, its conclusion refuted 'build param_to_calls to unblock removal', and the load-bearing unmeasured claim it names for itself -- that unconfirmed would stay ~0 among walks composition MAKES run, inferred from 0-of-28 among walks that run today -- still stands unmeasured, and measuring it requires the composition prototype the item says should not be built before the row-inflation cost is priced. That ordering is a decision, not a next step."  # 2449
